@@ -74,7 +74,16 @@ CREATE IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE CHARS ALLOT \ This space contains the target image.
 \ bisection, not fully root-caused - see PROGRESS.md). These are called
 \ often enough, from enough different contexts, that avoiding DO/LOOP's
 \ own return-stack usage entirely was the safer fix.
+\ Iteration 255: when a target cell is a cell of this host - the same width,
+\ and this host little-endian, so its @ and ! lay the bytes as the loops below
+\ do - @-T and !-T use them. The loops, a byte at a time, were 37% of the
+\ kernel workload's dispatches (the fastest design, without its JIT); the
+\ kernel they build is byte-identical. FAST-T is decided once, here, after
+\ TARGET-CELL-BYTES is set; a 4-byte target keeps the loops.
+VARIABLE FAST-T
+1 PAD ! PAD C@ 1 =  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 1 CELLS =  AND FAST-T !
 : @-T  ( t-addr --- x)
+  FAST-T @ IF CHARS IMAGE + @ EXIT THEN
   0 0
   BEGIN
     DUP TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ <
@@ -97,6 +106,7 @@ CREATE IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE CHARS ALLOT \ This space contains the target image.
     THEN
   THEN ;
 : !-T  ( x t-addr ---)
+  FAST-T @ IF CHARS IMAGE + ! EXIT THEN
   0
   BEGIN
     DUP TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ <
